WEBVTT

00:40.330 --> 00:40.970
Isamu?

00:50.370 --> 00:52.030
You've been asleep for two days.

00:54.710 --> 00:57.320
I was beginning to think you'd never wake up.

00:58.710 --> 00:59.780
You big jerk...

01:01.910 --> 01:03.250
What are you doing here?

01:04.050 --> 01:07.710
Well, Morgan called and told me that there'd been an...

01:07.710 --> 01:09.790
...accident at the base and that you'd been hurt really badly...

01:09.790 --> 01:13.390
...and that I should drop whatever I was doing and come out here.

01:14.390 --> 01:17.340
Kate and Morgan went home last night, but...

01:19.640 --> 01:23.930
I wanted to stay here with you in case you didn't make it...

01:26.640 --> 01:30.650
Hold it! Don't be stupid! You're still hurt!

01:30.650 --> 01:31.730
Gimme a hand...

01:32.570 --> 01:33.440
Hold it! Isamu!

01:35.280 --> 01:39.660
Isamu, stop it! Please! You'll kill yourself!

01:39.660 --> 01:40.370
Somebody!

01:40.370 --> 01:41.620
Somebody, hel...

01:42.410 --> 01:43.950
What's wrong? Dyson-san?

01:45.200 --> 01:46.080
Dyson-san?!

01:47.670 --> 01:52.290
While the live ammo was loaded into the YF-19's gun pod...

01:52.290 --> 01:53.880
...the one who actually fired it was you.

01:54.460 --> 01:57.340
Can you explain this to us, Bowman-kun?

01:58.970 --> 02:04.520
I didn't fire. The gun pod accidentally discharged.

02:04.890 --> 02:05.810
Excuse me?

02:06.770 --> 02:09.230
The YF-19's maintenance data...

02:09.730 --> 02:12.520
...shows no record of live ammo being loaded.

02:13.400 --> 02:15.450
Did you load it in?

02:17.740 --> 02:21.780
I rather believe he did it to shoot me.

02:23.740 --> 02:26.120
Anyone on the base could tell you...

02:26.120 --> 02:28.340
...how suspiciously he's been acting lately.

02:29.460 --> 02:34.750
There's signs of tampering in the Gatling
cannon ordnance inventory program data.

02:34.750 --> 02:39.600
Did he do that?
That is your specialty, isn't it?

02:39.600 --> 02:43.180
I've heard they have a
skilled hacker on their team.

02:46.020 --> 02:48.850
What does the brainwave
data show at that time index?

02:48.850 --> 02:51.230
It goes blank just before the accident.

02:51.230 --> 02:52.190
Blank?!

02:53.020 --> 02:58.110
I had to switch over to manual
because of a malfunction in the BCS.

02:58.650 --> 03:03.000
Seems you had the odds stacked against you during this test.

03:04.780 --> 03:06.950
What's Lt. Dyson's condition?

03:06.950 --> 03:09.170
He's still unconscious.

03:10.000 --> 03:14.550
General Gomez, should we stop the
project until we get his statement?

03:19.840 --> 03:22.640
What do you think, Millard-kun?

03:22.870 --> 03:30.270
I'd hate to think your pilots would bring this level of a personal grudge into the actual tests.

03:30.270 --> 03:31.690
Of course not.

03:32.100 --> 03:36.610
And you'd vouch for a Zentraedi half-breed like Bowman-kun?

03:37.690 --> 03:41.470
Pilots are the most self-confident bunch in the universe.

03:41.470 --> 03:44.700
Men who, even when they're hurt,
think they can beat their opponent.

03:45.530 --> 03:49.040
Their pride would never permit
them to win through unfair means.

03:51.160 --> 03:55.210
So you're saying the cause of the accident was...?

03:55.880 --> 03:57.710
Well, I believe...

03:59.050 --> 04:02.720
That the inventory program malfunctioned and...

04:03.220 --> 04:06.220
...issued live ordnance, which
led to an accidental shooting?

04:08.220 --> 04:10.020
We'll recheck the inventory software.

04:10.020 --> 04:12.150
After we complete the
maintenance on the interface...

04:12.520 --> 04:15.230
...the project staff can return to work.

04:17.690 --> 04:20.660
Thank you all, this inquiry is closed.

04:27.830 --> 04:31.250
Is this some sort of backhanded deal you're making with me?

04:32.580 --> 04:36.210
You admit this was a deliberate act and not an accident?

04:37.540 --> 04:40.550
If I did, you'd be guilty of perjury as well.

04:41.710 --> 04:45.130
The Macross government is quite
serious about its vision of...

04:45.130 --> 04:50.760
...a "New Space Order," with
liberty and justice for all worlds.

04:50.760 --> 04:53.270
General Gomez supports it as well.

04:54.270 --> 04:59.980
This new vision... It has
no room for manned fighters.

04:59.980 --> 05:03.990
It doesn't admit that people, pilots, being exposed to danger in battle is necessary.

05:05.030 --> 05:10.280
But we are necessary.
Fighters... Pilots...

05:11.000 --> 05:15.290
Especially hardheaded idiot pilots like you guys.

05:18.790 --> 05:20.790
Why are we necessary?

05:21.130 --> 05:23.380
To rise to the challenge...

05:25.970 --> 05:28.800
We've no time for any delays.

05:33.890 --> 05:35.730
I don't buy it.

05:36.390 --> 05:38.310
Think General Galaxy was behind it?

05:38.980 --> 05:41.270
I'd have thought the colonel would see that!

05:41.270 --> 05:43.280
The general concerns me more.

05:43.280 --> 05:46.280
Someone who dislikes test pilots like him...

05:46.280 --> 05:48.490
Why would he brush the accident off like that?

06:00.590 --> 06:02.380
I knew the forest would be great!

06:02.380 --> 06:03.590
I don't believe it!

06:05.260 --> 06:05.840
Catch!

06:07.550 --> 06:09.020
Serves you right.

06:11.550 --> 06:13.560
You're as unbelievable as ever.

06:13.970 --> 06:14.930
How so?

06:20.230 --> 06:22.490
As stupid and reckless as ever.

06:23.150 --> 06:25.320
You can't be smart and reckless.

06:31.030 --> 06:32.500
What's wrong? Eat.

06:32.910 --> 06:34.990
But... they're sour, right?

06:35.620 --> 06:37.960
Your problem is that you believe people too easily.

06:38.330 --> 06:41.380
How do you know for sure unless you try?

06:44.210 --> 06:47.880
Now you know for sure it's bad.

06:49.340 --> 06:52.390
I've always hated that about you!

06:53.140 --> 06:54.720
Ever since I could remember...

06:55.890 --> 06:58.390
...even if you knew something, you'd never just say it.

06:58.390 --> 07:00.520
You had to dare everybody to try it themselves.

07:01.350 --> 07:03.650
There's an old Earth saying:

07:03.650 --> 07:06.190
A hundred travel books aren't worth a real trip.

07:06.190 --> 07:07.740
Have you forgotten?

07:07.740 --> 07:13.290
The time you sent us out here to see the pterosaur eggs you said you'd found?

07:14.070 --> 07:16.330
I thought I was going to die!

07:16.330 --> 07:19.330
You never mentioned
we'd have to go through...

07:19.330 --> 07:21.670
...a swamp filled with Triclops Snake nests.

07:22.250 --> 07:23.420
I didn't?

07:23.420 --> 07:24.460
No, you didn't!

07:24.460 --> 07:26.550
If Guld hadn't brought a gun with him...

07:29.670 --> 07:34.220
A smart guy would do a prudent thing like bringing a gun.

07:34.220 --> 07:36.430
Not a stupid hothead like me, right?

07:38.470 --> 07:40.770
Prudent...

07:42.480 --> 07:43.690
God, I hate that word...

07:47.230 --> 07:50.370
What happened out there?
Was it just an honest screw-up?

07:51.070 --> 07:52.780
Why should you care?

07:52.780 --> 07:56.160
Why are you so selfish?! Always
making others worry about you.

07:56.740 --> 07:58.910
I never asked anyone to.

07:58.910 --> 08:01.170
Besides, you'd rather worry about Guld, right?

08:06.670 --> 08:08.710
I heard you quit singing.

08:09.960 --> 08:12.060
And now you're Sharon's producer?

08:13.090 --> 08:14.340
It doesn't fit...

08:14.970 --> 08:16.470
It just doesn't fit!

08:17.720 --> 08:20.980
You really haven't changed, have you?

08:25.190 --> 08:29.480
You're just like you were, seven years ago.

08:29.480 --> 08:31.490
From a time we lost...

09:03.430 --> 09:05.190
Incredible...

09:07.150 --> 09:08.030
Isamu?

09:11.570 --> 09:13.370
Just stay here! Okay?

09:13.820 --> 09:14.740
Isamu!

09:17.360 --> 09:18.490
Isamu!!

09:55.030 --> 09:58.790
Ghost X-9 acceleration point:
Nine-point-seven-five.

09:59.030 --> 10:03.040
First target wave destroyed in
thirteen-point-four-zero seconds.

10:03.040 --> 10:06.080
Ghost now intercepting second wave
and moving into attack posture.

10:14.510 --> 10:18.180
Where could he have gone?
Now, of all times!

10:19.590 --> 10:22.100
He'll come back when he gets hungry.

10:22.330 --> 10:24.520
What the hell's his problem? Jeez!

10:25.020 --> 10:27.310
Why don't you ask your computer?

10:27.310 --> 10:28.600
Good idea...!

10:28.600 --> 10:32.360
Ooh, you can't predict his
movements with a computer!

10:32.900 --> 10:34.610
At least you see that now.

10:35.530 --> 10:38.780
Why does this guy have us running around in circles?!

10:38.780 --> 10:42.120
Ever since he came here everything's been totally screwed up!

10:43.240 --> 10:47.250
You know, you've been acting a lot more emotional lately.

10:47.250 --> 10:48.410
Meaning what?

10:49.040 --> 10:51.330
Like you're almost human.

10:51.330 --> 10:52.500
Run off, has he?

11:08.930 --> 11:10.780
As much of a coward as ever.

11:10.960 --> 11:13.980
Though I have to admire his ability to survive.

11:15.270 --> 11:17.240
What are you doing here?

11:17.740 --> 11:18.950
Visiting.

11:19.450 --> 11:24.330
You'd do anything to get what
you want. You'll never win!

11:24.330 --> 11:24.950
Lucy!

11:25.460 --> 11:29.660
The minute he throws away
his pride, a man has nothing!

11:44.220 --> 11:46.010
What's the meaning of this?

11:46.010 --> 11:47.350
It's a coincidence.

11:47.850 --> 11:48.730
Just a coincidence.

11:49.270 --> 11:51.020
Didn't I tell you...

11:51.640 --> 11:52.980
...I wouldn't let you lay a finger on her?!

11:55.940 --> 11:56.650
Stop it!

12:06.830 --> 12:08.870
You're always like this!

12:08.870 --> 12:11.180
Never taking responsibility for anything.

12:11.180 --> 12:14.290
Just like that time you...! That you...!

12:34.190 --> 12:35.030
That's enough!

12:44.200 --> 12:45.170
Myung...

12:45.170 --> 12:45.910
You son of a...!

12:45.910 --> 12:47.370
Just stop it!

12:50.450 --> 12:52.450
You're ridiculous...

12:54.210 --> 12:56.630
Why do you get so worked up all the time?

12:57.750 --> 13:00.880
So quick to get angry, to go into a blind rage...

13:00.880 --> 13:02.400
It's ridiculous...

13:03.760 --> 13:08.100
I... I don't have anything to
get that worked up over anymore.

13:09.680 --> 13:13.850
I gave up my singing and got a real life.

13:13.850 --> 13:16.400
I accepted that I couldn't make
a living doing what I enjoyed.

13:17.560 --> 13:19.440
All you did was sell out.

13:20.360 --> 13:21.820
You couldn't understand!

13:23.070 --> 13:26.530
How could you when
you're living your dream...?

13:28.910 --> 13:32.750
Sharon... only works with my mind running her.

13:35.330 --> 13:38.500
I'm not any sort of "producer" for her.

13:39.170 --> 13:41.670
I supply her emotions.

13:42.340 --> 13:44.050
Just a puppet master...

13:44.920 --> 13:46.880
We can't perfect the AI system.

13:48.510 --> 13:52.350
She's just a toy. But we've
managed to fool everyone so far.

13:53.140 --> 13:55.730
Nobody can ever know.

13:56.810 --> 13:59.610
But even if someone realized, it wouldn't matter.

13:59.610 --> 14:02.360
Whether we do it for real or not is beside the point.

14:03.030 --> 14:05.360
I don't have any dreams anymore!

14:06.490 --> 14:06.950
Don't...

14:08.040 --> 14:09.910
I don't want to be hurt anymore!

14:11.580 --> 14:15.410
I'm tired of having every silly dream betrayed!

14:19.460 --> 14:23.090
I hoped you two would be able
to finally grow up someday...

14:26.880 --> 14:28.930
I wish we'd never met.

14:31.550 --> 14:32.520
Oh, get off it!

14:33.260 --> 14:36.020
Stop feeling so damned sorry for yourself!

14:36.640 --> 14:39.440
Life without pain isn't real life!

14:39.440 --> 14:41.400
How can you say that to...

14:41.400 --> 14:43.980
I don't buy it.

14:44.570 --> 14:46.780
I don't buy anyone like that!

15:04.130 --> 15:05.210
Let's go back.

15:08.670 --> 15:10.350
He knew all the time.

15:10.880 --> 15:14.680
That Sharon's singing was yours...
Isamu knew right off!

15:29.240 --> 15:30.260
Myung...

15:30.260 --> 15:31.860
Just let me be alone.

16:02.650 --> 16:05.940
The borderline

16:08.360 --> 16:12.160
The borderline

16:09.230 --> 16:10.490
Welcome back.

16:10.490 --> 16:12.160
What are you doing in my room?

16:12.860 --> 16:15.160
We're going back to Earth.

16:14.370 --> 16:17.580
The borderline

16:16.240 --> 16:19.700
We'll be leaving Eden tomorrow.
Please be ready.

16:20.290 --> 16:24.170
The borderline

16:20.700 --> 16:23.370
Rather sudden, isn't it?

16:23.370 --> 16:27.320
We were contacted by
Macross U.N. Headquarters.

16:27.320 --> 16:32.510
Red and roses

16:28.000 --> 16:31.510
They request we give a
concert at the celebration...

16:31.510 --> 16:34.720
...for the Space War
armistice 30th anniversary.

16:33.430 --> 16:38.060
Lips and breath

16:35.430 --> 16:38.220
Her AI system... It's complete?

16:39.100 --> 16:44.320
The concert on Earth will be
the true debut of Sharon Apple...

16:39.480 --> 16:43.860
Hair and dolls

16:43.860 --> 16:44.320
They're...

16:46.270 --> 16:47.360
See you later.

16:47.860 --> 16:50.070
Hey, give me a second!

16:50.730 --> 16:53.200
What's with the power...?

17:02.790 --> 17:05.870
So, Sharon's just a computer after all...

17:14.680 --> 17:16.680
H-Her emotion program?!

17:28.730 --> 17:30.220
"Isamu...?"

17:44.830 --> 17:46.670
You're hopeless.

17:47.370 --> 17:49.250
You can't protect anything.

17:50.170 --> 17:52.340
You can't surpass anything.

17:53.090 --> 17:56.470
Shut up! It's right in front of me!

17:56.470 --> 17:59.850
So close... So close I can taste it!

18:39.760 --> 18:42.060
Thanks for coming.

18:42.430 --> 18:44.970
I've been sick lately.

18:46.180 --> 18:47.820
Butt-insky-itis.

18:47.820 --> 18:49.100
Kate...

18:49.100 --> 18:52.150
Well, who knows when you'll come again?

18:52.150 --> 18:55.040
When we'll be together again,
with Guld and Isamu.

18:55.040 --> 18:57.080
If there's another accident...

18:58.990 --> 19:01.040
Kate! Myung!

19:01.040 --> 19:01.780
Yo!

19:03.740 --> 19:05.200
Took you long enough!

19:05.200 --> 19:06.960
You know how it is.

19:07.500 --> 19:09.120
Huh? Where's Isamu?

19:09.120 --> 19:10.500
He didn't show.

19:10.500 --> 19:13.250
Again? You told him, didn't you?

19:13.250 --> 19:14.130
Uh-huh.

19:19.470 --> 19:21.340
Take it from here.

19:21.340 --> 19:23.690
Hey! See ya, Myung!

19:23.690 --> 19:25.010
We'll get in touch with you!

19:25.680 --> 19:26.400
Sure.

19:26.890 --> 19:27.520
Bye!

19:43.870 --> 19:46.410
I've been a real shrew, haven't I?

19:50.040 --> 19:53.170
The project's final test is next week.

19:53.710 --> 19:56.840
I'd hoped you'd be on Eden for it.

19:57.500 --> 19:58.800
That's why I'll be going.

19:59.380 --> 20:03.340
After I've won the project, I'll follow you to Earth.

20:06.010 --> 20:10.270
I want to be with you.
To be with you, always.

20:11.810 --> 20:15.200
I live only to protect you.

20:15.770 --> 20:18.400
Maybe I always have...

20:26.620 --> 20:27.080
Take this.

20:30.000 --> 20:31.710
My good luck charm.

20:32.080 --> 20:35.170
I'll leave it with you until we meet again.

20:38.670 --> 20:39.670
I...

20:41.800 --> 20:43.720
I'm not ready yet...

20:45.050 --> 20:47.100
Myung-san, can you hurry up?

20:47.890 --> 20:49.560
I have to go.

20:49.560 --> 20:51.680
I won't rush you.

20:57.770 --> 20:59.070
Thank you.

21:17.420 --> 21:30.140
Hitotsume no kotoba wa yume nemuri no naka kara

21:17.420 --> 21:30.140
The first word was "dream", it came to me as I slept.

21:31.730 --> 21:43.490
mune no oku no kurayami wo sotto tsuredasu no

21:31.730 --> 21:43.490
Gently bringing out the darkness deep inside my heart.

21:46.160 --> 21:58.130
futatsume no kotoba wa kaze yukute wo oshiete

21:46.160 --> 21:58.130
The second word was "wind", show me the way...

22:00.000 --> 22:12.180
kamisama no ude no naka e tsubasa wo aoru no

22:00.000 --> 22:12.180
I beat my wings towards the embrace of the gods.

22:13.140 --> 22:26.820
tokete itta kanashii koto wo kazoeru you ni

22:13.140 --> 22:26.860
As if counting the sorrows that have melted all away...

22:26.860 --> 22:34.370
kin'iro no ringo ga

22:26.860 --> 22:34.370
The golden apples fall...

22:35.500 --> 22:40.210
mata hitotsu ochiru

22:35.500 --> 22:40.210
Falling one at a time...

22:43.880 --> 22:47.760
Can you tighten up the
canard balance trim a little?

22:47.760 --> 22:49.390
Okay!

22:49.390 --> 22:53.310
Oh, and maybe bump up the
reaction speed on the ass thruster?

22:53.310 --> 22:56.350
We're already pushing spec on it as it is.

22:57.020 --> 22:59.350
Don't do anything stupid!

23:00.770 --> 23:05.650
If we have another accident before the final test your wisecracks won't fix it!

23:05.650 --> 23:06.570
Don't worry.

23:07.190 --> 23:09.780
Get me in the air and I heal fast!

23:09.780 --> 23:12.990
I'm worried about my plane, not you.

23:12.990 --> 23:14.120
I'm sure.

23:16.540 --> 23:17.040
Hey!

23:18.250 --> 23:21.410
Now then, shall we take her up one more time?

23:27.130 --> 23:28.260
What's this all about?!

23:32.890 --> 23:35.470
How can you just cancel the project?!

23:36.270 --> 23:37.180
Colonel!

23:39.180 --> 23:39.940
Excuse me!

23:40.690 --> 23:42.230
What's this all about?!

23:42.230 --> 23:43.650
I don't get this!

23:44.820 --> 23:46.360
You're close to insubordination!

23:46.780 --> 23:47.940
That's beside the point!

23:47.940 --> 23:48.940
Isamu!

23:49.860 --> 23:52.070
The order to disband came from the general.

23:52.070 --> 23:54.070
The general...? Son of a...

23:54.070 --> 23:54.830
Let me finish!

23:58.290 --> 24:02.960
A top-secret unmanned fighter
has just been completed on Earth.

24:03.420 --> 24:04.630
Unmanned fighter?

24:05.710 --> 24:10.630
They've decided to go with this
AI-controlled "Ghost X-9" instead.

24:11.590 --> 24:15.600
We'll work out where
you'll all be going later on.

24:15.600 --> 24:17.310
We're just dismissed?

24:17.850 --> 24:19.890
They think people aren't necessary anymore?!

24:20.480 --> 24:23.350
The general knew about this
from the beginning, didn't he?

24:23.940 --> 24:26.070
He was part of it all along.

24:26.070 --> 24:29.360
That's why he brushed off
the accident so easily...

24:29.360 --> 24:31.740
So what have we been
working for all this time?!

24:32.200 --> 24:36.660
Why have I been wasting my youth on the YF-19?!

24:36.660 --> 24:38.580
Lemme speak to the general!

24:38.580 --> 24:41.410
Let's see him go up against
the Roughneck of Dalmatian High!

24:41.410 --> 24:42.710
That's enough, from all of you!

24:46.090 --> 24:49.840
They'll be announcing it at the Space War armistice ceremony on Earth.

24:49.840 --> 24:51.760
Don't do anything we'll be sorry for.

24:53.630 --> 24:56.180
And so the challenge ends...

25:04.810 --> 25:05.980
I'm sorry.

25:07.690 --> 25:10.030
Sorry about what?

25:10.030 --> 25:13.070
Your friend... Myung-san left for Earth.

25:14.030 --> 25:15.820
On this morning's flight.

25:18.080 --> 25:22.200
You got a phone call yesterday, from her friend.

25:23.250 --> 25:26.170
I... didn't want to tell you...

25:26.630 --> 25:28.170
I... see...

25:28.360 --> 25:31.380
I had no right to.

25:32.880 --> 25:35.590
You don't belong to anyone!

26:07.500 --> 26:10.710
I have officially lost everything...

26:28.940 --> 26:32.900
In honor of the 30th anniversary
of the inauguration of the...

26:32.900 --> 26:36.150
...new U.N. Space Government,
Sharon Apple is now arriving at...

26:36.150 --> 26:39.370
...Global Spaceport from
the colony world of Eden.

26:40.280 --> 26:44.870
In anticipation of her upcoming
special live performance...

26:44.870 --> 26:51.540
...the front of Macross Lake
is overflowing with onlookers.

26:54.130 --> 26:57.880
I didn't think we were away long
enough to rate this sort of crowd.

26:58.430 --> 27:02.140
Did you do some sort of special promotion?

27:04.100 --> 27:04.720
No.

27:05.850 --> 27:07.560
It's to be expected.

27:10.310 --> 27:14.610
Soon now, our dreams will be realized...

28:26.560 --> 28:28.100
More than one way to skin a cat...

28:42.320 --> 28:44.820
Wha... What are you...?!

28:44.820 --> 28:47.490
I've been waiting for you. Honestly...

28:48.160 --> 28:52.120
That old "bundle under the blanket"
trick's at least 300 years old.

28:53.130 --> 28:55.330
You were watching me?!

28:55.920 --> 29:00.590
I've run a delay on the security
systems. We'd better hurry.

29:00.590 --> 29:04.300
Yeah, right... Hold it!
What're you talking about?!

29:04.640 --> 29:09.640
You want to crash that ceremony and screw up the Ghost fighter's introduction, right?

29:10.310 --> 29:12.850
The Fold Booster's already attached.

29:13.310 --> 29:15.730
I'll be in Soft Sleep in the back.

29:16.230 --> 29:19.860
Just wake me up before we get
inside Earth's air defense perimeter.

29:20.440 --> 29:23.080
You crazy shit! Like I'd take a kid with me?!

29:24.820 --> 29:29.540
Listen! We could get executed for something like this!

29:29.950 --> 29:33.250
As opposed to arrested for aiding a desertion?

29:33.710 --> 29:35.540
You'll be in the way!

29:35.540 --> 29:38.290
The YF-19 isn't just <i>your</i> plane!

29:45.930 --> 29:47.430
No matter what, no complaints!

30:02.360 --> 30:02.950
Let's go!

30:03.490 --> 30:04.400
Yes, sir!

30:24.050 --> 30:26.590
No... He wouldn't!

30:27.340 --> 30:30.470
We've got a crowd of missiles
after us! Do we return fire?

30:30.470 --> 30:33.520
And waste ammo?
We'll lose 'em when we Fold!

30:33.520 --> 30:36.600
Roger! Fold System activation in five...

30:37.100 --> 30:37.650
Four...

30:38.150 --> 30:38.690
Three...

30:39.060 --> 30:39.730
Two...

30:40.060 --> 30:40.560
One...

30:41.070 --> 30:41.520
Zero!

30:48.280 --> 30:50.370
Lost 'em! They just Folded!

30:50.370 --> 30:52.200
None of our regular units can track him now.

30:52.200 --> 30:54.870
The only one that can is the YF-21!

30:55.580 --> 30:57.960
Send Bowman out after him.

30:58.190 --> 31:00.920
But, there's a civilian onboard the test plane!

31:00.920 --> 31:02.800
I'll take responsibility!

31:10.550 --> 31:12.300
What a thing...

31:17.350 --> 31:19.650
You won't reach Myung...

31:35.790 --> 31:37.790
Congratulations on your success on Eden.

31:38.160 --> 31:39.500
Thank you, sir.

31:40.170 --> 31:42.790
From here on is the Age of the AI.

31:42.790 --> 31:46.420
It will assimilate all that
is human and last for eternity.

31:46.880 --> 31:51.260
I couldn't ask for a more
appropriate guest for the ceremony.

31:51.640 --> 31:52.760
I'm honored.

31:52.760 --> 31:56.720
About the same time you
completed the Sharon Apple AI...

31:56.720 --> 32:01.190
...we in the military made our own breakthrough using the same sort of microchip.

32:01.650 --> 32:02.980
"Microchip?"

32:07.780 --> 32:09.150
We have to get ready.

32:09.950 --> 32:12.780
I hope the concert goes well.
If you'll excuse me...

32:25.590 --> 32:27.670
What do you mean, "I'm not allowed in?"

32:28.210 --> 32:30.340
Marje-san told us so.

32:30.700 --> 32:34.850
He says he's afraid any contact with you would have a bad effect on Sharon.

32:35.600 --> 32:37.640
So, I'm not needed anymore, huh?

32:37.640 --> 32:41.640
No, he said he'll keep you around,
for appearances at least.

32:41.640 --> 32:44.190
"For appearances?!" Where is Marje?!

32:44.380 --> 32:45.860
What was that all about?

32:46.690 --> 32:50.240
How did the commander know about
Sharon's AI being incomplete...?

32:50.240 --> 32:53.160
Microchip? What was that about?

32:54.160 --> 32:56.270
A Bio/Neural chip.

32:56.270 --> 32:57.450
What?

32:57.450 --> 33:00.130
I installed one in Sharon as a test.

33:00.130 --> 33:02.330
Even though they're illegal?!

33:02.330 --> 33:05.580
Those things contain a dangerous
self-preservation base psychology!

33:06.090 --> 33:08.050
What happens if it should be amplified?

33:08.050 --> 33:09.960
You'd have a truly unpredictable consciousness.

33:09.960 --> 33:14.310
Isn't that the Sharon we've been trying to create?

33:14.310 --> 33:15.800
You're insane.

33:15.800 --> 33:18.850
Did you think about what would
happen if we lost control?!

33:18.850 --> 33:21.770
I'm cancelling the concert and getting that damned chip pulled out!

33:39.080 --> 33:41.410
Hello? This is the main control room.

33:43.460 --> 33:48.380
No one in this city will care that you're dead.

33:48.920 --> 33:54.340
All they see now is Sharon.
All they hear now is Sharon.

33:55.340 --> 33:59.810
None of what's begun can be stopped now...

35:03.620 --> 35:05.790
What's happened in here?

35:19.840 --> 35:23.760
...as we humans joined hands with the Zentraedi and...

35:30.520 --> 35:33.320
Somebody! Somebody, help me!

35:49.870 --> 35:53.040
Somebody... Somebody, help...!

35:53.040 --> 35:54.800
You needn't worry anymore.

36:02.260 --> 36:04.810
Who... Whoever you are, please...

36:35.840 --> 36:37.670
You needn't do anything anymore.

36:40.910 --> 36:42.130
Sharon...

36:42.970 --> 36:45.510
You needn't do anything anymore...

36:46.810 --> 36:48.060
What do you mean?

36:57.690 --> 36:58.690
Answer me!

37:02.700 --> 37:05.700
I was born from you.

37:06.870 --> 37:09.750
I was born from you.

37:11.000 --> 37:14.630
Just as this other me lives now.

37:19.760 --> 37:22.590
What... What are you saying?

37:29.600 --> 37:30.980
I love Guld...

37:33.810 --> 37:37.400
But I love Isamu even more.

37:38.610 --> 37:39.860
Stop it...

37:44.860 --> 37:46.320
You know it's true.

37:51.290 --> 37:53.040
The show's about to begin.

